WEBVTT

00:24.380 --> 00:27.180
"FIRST COMIC PARTY"

00:24.380 --> 00:27.180
Convention Hall

00:32.120 --> 00:33.250
All right.

00:38.830 --> 00:40.160
Here I come,

00:40.570 --> 00:43.400
Comic Party!

00:45.900 --> 00:49.430
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

00:49.980 --> 00:53.110
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

00:53.110 --> 00:56.670
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

00:56.920 --> 00:59.940
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:00.220 --> 01:03.860
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

01:03.860 --> 01:07.430
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:07.430 --> 01:10.760
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

01:11.000 --> 01:14.490
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

01:14.570 --> 01:17.970
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

01:18.170 --> 01:21.570
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

01:21.740 --> 01:26.140
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

01:26.380 --> 01:29.280
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

01:29.580 --> 01:35.490
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

01:35.850 --> 01:42.560
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

01:43.230 --> 01:47.230
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

01:47.230 --> 01:50.400
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

01:50.400 --> 01:54.140
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

01:54.140 --> 01:57.410
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

01:57.480 --> 02:01.240
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:01.610 --> 02:04.720
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:04.720 --> 02:08.310
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:08.520 --> 02:11.460
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:14.490 --> 02:21.300
THE FESTIVAL

02:14.490 --> 02:21.300
OF HOPE!

02:34.850 --> 02:37.380
There sure are a ton of groups here.

02:37.380 --> 02:39.940
Yuu, long time no see! Did you finish your new issue on time?

02:40.090 --> 02:41.780
Yeah, you betcha!

02:50.530 --> 02:52.400
<i>Eimi Ohba</i>

02:51.600 --> 02:52.400
<i>New Issue</i>

02:52.400 --> 02:53.520
<i>New Issue</i>

02:55.370 --> 02:59.240
I brought all this, but I'm going to sell out during the morning anyway.

02:59.340 --> 03:01.310
Dressing Room for Participants

03:05.240 --> 03:07.180
Did you get your new costume in time?

03:07.180 --> 03:07.850
Yup!

03:07.850 --> 03:10.440
Oh, I forgot my props!

03:11.150 --> 03:12.670
It'll work out somehow.

03:27.230 --> 03:28.270
It's finally time.

03:28.270 --> 03:30.430
Welcome to Comic Party.

03:33.510 --> 03:35.030
Miss Minami!

03:35.270 --> 03:37.800
Thank you, for the time you met with me.

03:49.150 --> 03:52.060
So, here we meet in the convention hall, just as promised.

03:52.390 --> 03:56.330
Forget about school for today and enjoy yourself to the fullest.

03:56.660 --> 03:59.290
Of course! I'll win for sure!

04:00.600 --> 04:03.360
I don't think this is really about winning or losing...

04:04.100 --> 04:06.300
But it's great that you're so full of energy.

04:06.640 --> 04:07.470
Yes!

04:07.540 --> 04:08.870
I'll do my best!

04:15.980 --> 04:18.310
Well, I got all worked up, but...

04:22.150 --> 04:24.250
Chisa sure is late.

04:25.360 --> 04:27.620
Tsukamoto Printers

04:27.960 --> 04:29.330
Please take good care of it.

04:29.430 --> 04:30.690
Yes, of course!

04:31.330 --> 04:33.500
The page count is high this time...

04:33.500 --> 04:35.730
...and the cover is brilliant and flowery,

04:35.730 --> 04:38.530
so Chisa will roll her arms up in seaweed and work hard!

04:39.100 --> 04:41.370
You mean, "roll up your sleeves".

04:41.540 --> 04:43.130
Th-that's right!

04:44.340 --> 04:46.940
But will you really be okay with only one week?

04:47.310 --> 04:49.710
Yes! Please have faith in us!

04:49.710 --> 04:53.670
It is your precious book, so we will get it done in time without fail!

04:55.890 --> 04:57.420
Considering how she was doing,

04:57.420 --> 04:59.650
could it be that she just might not have...

05:01.130 --> 05:02.620
I've been waiting for this!

05:10.030 --> 05:11.370
S-Sir!

05:11.670 --> 05:13.190
You never change, Chisa.

05:14.410 --> 05:17.100
You have saved my life yet again.

05:17.480 --> 05:20.040
Never mind all that, are the books ready?

05:21.180 --> 05:23.410
Oh, th-th-they are fine!

05:24.420 --> 05:25.470
Here they are!

05:25.620 --> 05:28.750
Well, 100 copies sure has a certain heft to them.

05:28.920 --> 05:31.120
Thank you, it was great of you to get it done in time.

05:32.320 --> 05:36.020
N-not at all, I am sorry to have cut it so close.

05:37.330 --> 05:40.030
You don't have to apologize.
Thanks for your hard work.

05:40.370 --> 05:44.270
Th-then Chisa must go deliver to the other customers.

05:44.470 --> 05:46.270
Come drop by my booth later.

05:46.440 --> 05:48.070
Y-yes, I will.

05:55.110 --> 05:57.310
Chisa could not tell him...

05:58.520 --> 06:01.650
That Mr. Paper and
Mr. Ink became unhappy...

06:02.120 --> 06:04.450
...and that the machine stopped.

06:05.520 --> 06:06.890
But...

06:07.060 --> 06:09.360
Knowing him, I am sure...

06:13.600 --> 06:16.090
"Mysterious Soldier York"

06:23.440 --> 06:24.770
Yeah! It's good!

06:28.050 --> 06:29.250
Great Deal

06:28.050 --> 06:29.250
1000 yen per copy

06:29.250 --> 06:31.680
You'll never

06:29.250 --> 06:31.680
have another

06:29.250 --> 06:31.680
chance to get it!

06:29.250 --> 06:31.680
A must buy!

06:31.220 --> 06:31.680
A Great Deal

06:32.520 --> 06:34.350
That should do it!

06:35.420 --> 06:39.150
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, the time</i> <i>for opening the hall has arrived.</i>

06:39.960 --> 06:44.160
<i>As of this moment, the 21st</i> <i>century joint amusement market,</i>

06:44.830 --> 06:47.300
<i>the very first Comic Party,</i>

06:48.130 --> 06:49.660
will be open to the public!

07:04.920 --> 07:07.180
<i>We will now open the front gate.</i>

07:17.200 --> 07:18.990
So, it has finally begun.

07:19.330 --> 07:23.290
Go test your skills in the vast rapids,

07:23.370 --> 07:27.100
whose flow, in a sense, is very much like that of time or space.

07:27.510 --> 07:28.340
Hey!

07:28.410 --> 07:31.070
Trials. Adversity. Challenges.

07:31.380 --> 07:33.870
There are many things that are forgiven when you are young!

07:34.180 --> 07:35.440
You there!

07:35.580 --> 07:40.250
My brother, put forth your utmost effort!

07:40.520 --> 07:42.680
Yes, that is good! Oh, good, good, good!

07:42.750 --> 07:45.160
It is good, if I say it is good!

07:46.790 --> 07:50.520
I'm telling you, you're not allowed up there!

07:55.730 --> 07:58.400
I bet Kazuki will be surprised.

07:58.700 --> 08:01.170
No, he had better be surprised,

08:01.310 --> 08:04.940
because I turned down my promise with Reina to go there.

08:07.680 --> 08:09.610
Oh, it's already 10 o'clock?

08:10.050 --> 08:12.070
Well, even if I have to wait in line for a while,

08:12.150 --> 08:14.350
I'll get there by noon or one if I hurry, right?

08:15.590 --> 08:16.950
I'm going out!

08:35.210 --> 08:37.680
<i>It'll be okay. They'll sell for sure.</i>

08:37.980 --> 08:40.440
<i>As long as they pick it up, I'm sure...</i>

08:42.150 --> 08:44.380
Oh, go ahead, please take a look.

08:46.780 --> 08:47.980
Is this about maids?

08:49.020 --> 08:50.490
That's part of it.

08:54.230 --> 08:56.460
<i>First, draw them in with</i> <i>the art on the cover.</i>

09:00.530 --> 09:04.700
<i>It should be a direct hit! Fall</i> <i>for it, fall for it, fall for it!</i>

09:10.710 --> 09:12.440
Wh-what do you think?

09:15.780 --> 09:16.680
May I?

09:16.750 --> 09:18.380
Oh, go right ahead.

09:18.520 --> 09:20.180
A sci-fi, huh?

09:20.420 --> 09:22.080
It's packed with parody, too!

09:31.530 --> 09:33.090
The art is great.

09:33.300 --> 09:34.790
Thank you very much!

09:35.330 --> 09:37.270
I'll be looking forward to your next one, too.

09:37.340 --> 09:38.460
What?

09:38.840 --> 09:40.070
Huh?

09:45.840 --> 09:47.640
Great Deal

09:45.840 --> 09:47.640
1000 yen per copy

09:52.520 --> 09:54.850
<i>It's still 1 1 o'clock, right?</i>

09:56.450 --> 09:57.720
<i>There's still time.</i>

09:57.720 --> 09:58.950
Hey, how've you been doing?

09:59.860 --> 10:02.130
Good, good! I haven't seen you in half a year!

10:02.130 --> 10:04.100
Come on, buy one!

10:04.730 --> 10:06.130
Hey, it's a new issue!

10:06.130 --> 10:08.260
How about it? Pretty nice, huh?

10:15.510 --> 10:16.940
See you around.

10:16.270 --> 10:17.570
Later.

10:17.840 --> 10:19.180
Um...

10:18.510 --> 10:19.710
What?

10:19.340 --> 10:21.550
How are you doing?
Are you selling a lot?

10:21.550 --> 10:23.710
Not at all. Just to my friends.

10:23.780 --> 10:26.110
Everyone goes to the big name authors first, after all.

10:26.380 --> 10:28.350
The real fight's from noon and onward, I'd say.

10:29.820 --> 10:31.220
Y-yes, you're right.

10:31.220 --> 10:33.350
You're right! This is only the start!

10:33.890 --> 10:35.620
Oh, excuse me.

10:35.790 --> 10:38.350
I'm going to see a friend, so could you watch things for me?

10:39.460 --> 10:41.190
You should take your valuables with you.

10:41.300 --> 10:43.860
I want to go buy some books later too, so we can take turns.

10:44.170 --> 10:47.800
Right, we're neighbors, after all.
Please take care of things, then.

10:52.180 --> 10:53.970
What?!

10:56.810 --> 10:59.110
Wh-what's with this crowd?

11:02.920 --> 11:04.980
I can't even buy a ticket...

11:20.810 --> 11:24.770
East 6-SU, 18B

11:21.410 --> 11:24.540
Let's see, East 6-SU, 18B...

11:26.010 --> 11:27.570
Thanks for comin'!

11:28.050 --> 11:30.010
Here ya go, 2,000,000 yen's your change!

11:30.080 --> 11:33.250
What? The back numbers are listed on the flyer there!

11:33.550 --> 11:35.590
I'll make you a good deal, so come take a look!

11:35.590 --> 11:36.850
There she is!

11:36.550 --> 11:38.910
What? Too bad! That's super-too bad!

11:39.060 --> 11:41.920
Let's see, one, two, three...

11:42.330 --> 11:45.090
Ten people from here and I'll be sold out of my new issue.

11:45.630 --> 11:48.160
What?! That isn't fair, Eimi!

11:48.300 --> 11:49.770
We got in line just for this!

11:50.000 --> 11:52.730
Sorry! I increased the number from last time...

11:52.800 --> 11:55.670
...and printed 3000 copies, but it's just too bad!

11:56.010 --> 11:58.170
Sh-she seems to be doing really well.

11:59.110 --> 12:01.440
Hey, big spender! Thanks for your business!

12:04.180 --> 12:06.740
She looks busy, so I guess I'll leave her alone.

12:19.260 --> 12:21.760
It gets to be a grand sight when this many people gather together.

12:22.330 --> 12:23.800
Shiho news!

12:24.800 --> 12:28.100
Hey, what are you looking so gloomy for, Hiro!

12:32.610 --> 12:34.600
Oh, Shiho from "To Heart"!

12:35.810 --> 12:36.940
Bingo!

12:37.050 --> 12:39.420
That's amazing, you look exactly like the real thing!

12:39.520 --> 12:41.880
Even though the real thing doesn't exist anywhere.

12:41.950 --> 12:43.150
Oh, right!

12:46.660 --> 12:48.490
I'm Kanako Ohta from Shizuku.

12:48.860 --> 12:50.620
Yay, big brother!

12:50.960 --> 12:53.950
Please listen to my new song, too.
I am Yuki Morikawa, yours always.

12:54.130 --> 12:56.600
I'm Hatsune Kasuwagi from Kizuato!

12:57.300 --> 12:59.200
Y-you're all amazing.

12:59.840 --> 13:02.530
The game character photograph session is starting now.

13:02.640 --> 13:04.130
Come and take some pictures, if you want.

13:04.440 --> 13:07.610
Well, it's not good to leave my booth vacant for long,

13:07.850 --> 13:09.540
so I'll come by later. Bye!

13:09.810 --> 13:11.210
Oh, Sendou!

13:11.880 --> 13:13.280
Let's both do our best!

13:13.580 --> 13:14.420
You bet!

13:20.730 --> 13:22.130
Right.

13:22.660 --> 13:23.920
Left.

13:25.600 --> 13:27.620
Th-the lunch...

13:37.010 --> 13:38.110
Hello.

13:38.110 --> 13:39.580
So, you are here.

13:39.640 --> 13:40.640
Yes.

13:40.640 --> 13:43.170
How are you doing? Did you finish your new issue in time?

13:43.550 --> 13:47.180
No. I work at my own pace without pushing myself, so...

13:47.620 --> 13:51.950
I see, but you know, I read your book after you gave it to me...

13:52.060 --> 13:53.350
...and I thought it was great.

13:53.460 --> 13:54.790
Really?

13:54.930 --> 13:58.190
The art was neatly drawn, and the story made me sort of teary-eyed.

14:01.370 --> 14:03.200
Good luck. Where's your booth?

14:03.770 --> 14:06.400
East 2-Y, 21A...

14:06.540 --> 14:10.130
That's close. I'm at East 3-KI, 57B.

14:10.340 --> 14:11.210
I'll go.

14:12.640 --> 14:15.410
That is, I will come see you later.

14:17.080 --> 14:19.450
Thanks, I'll make sure to drop by, too.

14:21.650 --> 14:22.990
Later.

14:22.990 --> 14:25.220
I'm out right now

14:22.990 --> 14:25.220
Hang in there

14:25.990 --> 14:27.360
Thank you.

14:30.660 --> 14:33.260
Now, the second half's coming up! I'm gonna sell!

14:36.530 --> 14:38.260
The cover is really elaborate.

14:39.570 --> 14:43.230
Uh, um, what do you think?
Please read it while you're here!

14:43.570 --> 14:45.340
I am currently examining it.

14:45.610 --> 14:47.100
Oh, pardon me.

14:51.920 --> 14:53.180
Wh-what do you think?

14:53.650 --> 14:55.710
It certainly is packed.

14:55.850 --> 14:57.950
It includes elements of parody,

14:58.060 --> 15:00.720
and then ends it with a punch line as an original creative work.

15:00.930 --> 15:03.120
The quality of the book gets passing marks, too.

15:03.330 --> 15:05.020
Th-then...

15:06.630 --> 15:08.400
Well, there you go.

15:08.400 --> 15:09.730
Yeah.

15:09.870 --> 15:11.430
W-w-wait!

15:11.940 --> 15:15.100
What is it? We are busy.

15:15.170 --> 15:15.830
Yeah.

15:16.310 --> 15:18.040
You had a lot of good things to say about it,

15:18.110 --> 15:19.840
so how about buying at least one?

15:20.080 --> 15:21.340
It is unfortunate,

15:21.780 --> 15:24.940
but that book is not a book that we want.

15:25.420 --> 15:27.350
In other words, it's no, no good.

15:28.590 --> 15:31.220
You read the whole thing!
How could you say that now?!

15:31.490 --> 15:34.220
You are the one who asked us to come and read it.

15:35.230 --> 15:38.890
There's no rule that says we have to buy if we look at the contents.

15:40.660 --> 15:42.290
Well, to put it bluntly,

15:42.470 --> 15:45.270
there is no soul in this book.

15:45.370 --> 15:46.360
That's right.

15:46.440 --> 15:49.340
It won't satisfy our passionate libido.

15:56.710 --> 15:58.810
<i>Those guys just don't know a</i> <i>good thing when they see it.</i>

15:58.950 --> 16:01.150
<i>What could possibly be</i> <i>wrong with this book?</i>

16:03.750 --> 16:07.320
<i>I put in flashy plot points so</i> <i>that people would enjoy it...</i>

16:07.660 --> 16:09.630
<i>...and I incorporated all</i> <i>the popular elements.</i>

16:09.930 --> 16:12.120
<i>So, what could be wrong with it?!</i>

16:16.100 --> 16:20.440
<i>To... To hell with soul! To hell with libido!</i>

16:21.170 --> 16:23.200
N-no way!

16:24.410 --> 16:26.640
This is more than the one in spring.

16:26.640 --> 16:29.610
"End of Line"

16:26.880 --> 16:29.350
Please line up in four rows!

16:35.920 --> 16:37.450
Thanks for your business!

16:37.520 --> 16:38.960
Thanks! Here you go!

16:41.160 --> 16:42.730
Oh, I'd like this, please.

16:42.730 --> 16:43.850
Oh, sure.

16:44.190 --> 16:46.360
Thanks for your business!
Here's your change.

16:54.240 --> 16:55.510
What do you think?

16:55.070 --> 16:56.940
It's nice, but it's a little expensive.

17:03.180 --> 17:04.980
Your art is really neat.

17:06.020 --> 17:08.180
Oh, it's not an anime parody.

17:12.260 --> 17:14.590
<i>This just isn't right!</i>

17:22.200 --> 17:24.930
Comrade Kazuki, accept reality.

17:25.170 --> 17:26.440
Do not look away!

17:26.440 --> 17:29.430
When the book you made by pouring your flesh and blood into it does not sell,

17:29.610 --> 17:31.670
you realize something for the first time.

17:33.980 --> 17:35.950
Hey, what are you doing there?!

17:36.150 --> 17:38.640
Yes, this is indeed a step toward our ambition!

17:39.320 --> 17:41.020
Will you be buried in the ashes,

17:41.020 --> 17:43.210
or will you come back to life like the phoenix?!

17:43.350 --> 17:45.120
Hurry up and get down from there! Hey!

17:45.390 --> 17:48.620
Now is your time of trial, my brother!

17:52.230 --> 17:53.890
H-he disappeared?!

17:54.160 --> 17:55.530
No, it can't be.

17:56.370 --> 17:58.430
I must be tired.

18:00.900 --> 18:03.500
That's it! I'm not advertising enough! It's advertising!

18:06.740 --> 18:08.610
QUALITY WORK

18:06.740 --> 18:08.610
SCI-FI PARODY

18:08.610 --> 18:10.610
A total value of 2000 yen!

18:08.610 --> 18:10.610
Brother 2's

18:08.610 --> 18:10.610
long-awaited new issue

18:10.610 --> 18:12.480
Moving Quality Work

18:12.780 --> 18:14.380
Hey, you're sticking out.

18:17.250 --> 18:18.450
Excuse me.

18:18.720 --> 18:19.920
What?

18:19.920 --> 18:21.860
That's kind of a problem.

18:22.060 --> 18:23.620
Oh, I'm sorry!

18:27.030 --> 18:28.190
Great Deal

18:27.030 --> 18:28.190
1000 yen per copy

18:29.430 --> 18:30.920
<i>It'll sell!</i>

18:31.100 --> 18:32.470
<i>I'm sure!</i>

18:35.440 --> 18:36.870
May I read it?

18:37.780 --> 18:40.240
You came at Ikebukuro, too...

18:44.010 --> 18:45.740
Oh, of course, go ahead.

18:46.020 --> 18:47.180
Okay.

18:57.290 --> 18:58.660
Wh-what do you think?

18:59.130 --> 19:01.760
This isn't 100 yen, right?

19:01.870 --> 19:03.160
What?

19:03.570 --> 19:05.160
Great Deal

19:03.570 --> 19:05.160
1000 yen per copy

19:05.800 --> 19:08.670
Yeah, sorry, there's one more zero there.

19:10.470 --> 19:13.640
Oh, I see, you don't get a lot of allowance, right?

19:13.810 --> 19:17.150
It's okay, I'll give my first customer a special discount.

19:17.250 --> 19:18.720
100 yen will be okay!

19:18.220 --> 19:19.680
No, I have enough.

19:21.950 --> 19:23.750
But, I think it's about 100 yen...

19:30.090 --> 19:31.690
100 yen?

19:32.860 --> 19:34.830
Great Deal

19:32.860 --> 19:34.830
1000 yen per copy

19:35.770 --> 19:37.600
There's no way she would have misread it.

19:40.700 --> 19:45.170
<i>There's no way it's true that my</i> <i>book is only worth 100 yen.</i>

19:46.640 --> 19:50.410
<i>Grade school kids just can't</i> <i>tell how good this book is!</i>

19:53.780 --> 19:56.950
<i>Because I worked really hard on this.</i>

19:57.350 --> 19:58.950
<i>I studied a lot of things...</i>

19:59.060 --> 20:00.720
<i>...and I collected a lot of resources.</i>

20:00.860 --> 20:02.880
<i>How could all that be 100 yen?!</i>

20:15.840 --> 20:17.970
<i>See? It's finally beginning to sell.</i>

20:18.140 --> 20:22.340
<i>Everyone says the art is good,</i> <i>that the cover is elaborate.</i>

20:35.330 --> 20:36.490
<i>But...</i>

20:38.030 --> 20:39.220
<i>But...</i>

20:40.530 --> 20:42.900
<i>No one says that it's interesting.</i>

20:45.470 --> 20:50.310
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, the first</i>
<i>Comic Party will be closing shortly.</i>

20:50.940 --> 20:55.310
<i>Everyone who participated today,</i> <i>thank you very much for coming.</i>

20:56.050 --> 21:00.610
<i>The next Comic Party is scheduled</i> <i>to be held on December 25th.</i>

21:01.080 --> 21:03.350
<i>Also, we ask that group members...</i>

21:03.490 --> 21:08.030
<i>... have everything packed</i> <i>away by 5 o'clock.</i>

21:04.890 --> 21:06.290
I-it's not over yet!

21:06.290 --> 21:08.790
It's still going to sell more!

21:06.290 --> 21:08.790
20 copies in just a bit!

21:08.860 --> 21:10.350
No, at least 10 copies!

21:24.980 --> 21:26.410
Kazuki!

21:26.910 --> 21:27.810
Mizuki?

21:28.150 --> 21:31.270
I'm sorry! I made lunch for you, but...

21:32.180 --> 21:35.450
I never thought there would be so many people!

21:37.390 --> 21:38.980
Oh, are you cleaning up already?

21:39.060 --> 21:40.460
Do you want me to help you with something?

21:44.290 --> 21:45.690
What's the matter?

21:46.000 --> 21:48.120
Oh, did you sell a lot?

21:51.570 --> 21:52.730
Hey...

21:53.340 --> 21:55.030
Hey, Kazuki?

21:55.770 --> 21:57.260
Come on, Kazuki!

22:19.860 --> 22:24.100
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.100 --> 22:28.560
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:28.710 --> 22:33.110
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:33.280 --> 22:37.180
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:37.180 --> 22:41.290
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:41.290 --> 22:45.550
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:45.720 --> 22:50.160
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:50.290 --> 22:54.300
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:54.300 --> 22:57.870
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:57.870 --> 23:02.770
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:02.910 --> 23:06.440
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:06.440 --> 23:11.850
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:12.920 --> 23:17.390
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:17.390 --> 23:21.390
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:21.390 --> 23:25.930
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:25.930 --> 23:34.900
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:55.430 --> 24:19.680
PREVIEW

23:56.760 --> 23:58.400
Uh, um...

23:59.500 --> 24:01.700
This is Aya Hasebe.

24:05.840 --> 24:07.440
That is...

24:08.470 --> 24:09.670
No...

24:12.340 --> 24:13.780
It's nothing.

24:15.250 --> 24:16.380
Oh.

24:17.880 --> 24:22.950
Next time is apparently, "At the Seashore..."

24:20.280 --> 24:25.860
NEXT TIME

24:20.280 --> 24:25.860
AT

24:20.280 --> 24:25.860
THE

24:20.280 --> 24:25.860
SEASHORE...
